### H1 (SLOW SCANS)
- **Operator Belief:** Scan completion is slow primarily due to Ledger claim/release mismatches + wave-loop sync overhead, NOT simply because "full coverage takes time."
- **Synthesizer Verdict:** **PARTIAL (Dominant Causes Reframed)**
- **Evidence & Findings:**
  1. *Sync Overhead Refuted:* DB sync overhead across wave boundaries is measured at 40–50 ms per wave boundary against ~3,000 s wave durations (0.0015% of wave time) `[AGENT falcon-02:ws1_throughput/REPORT.md; mako-02:ws1_throughput/WS1-REPORT.md]`.
  2. *Historical Mismatch Patched on Batch Path:* The B1 worker_id mismatch (claiming under `"wave{N}"` and releasing under `"batch{w}-{id}-{model}"` freeing 0 rows) is already patched on the live batch path via `release_cells_by_ids` `[CONTEXT §5.2 B1; AGENT lynx-01:FINAL-REPORT.md; viper-01:REPORT.md]`.
  3. *Real Dominator 1 — Worker Dispatch Grind:* ~83–95% of total scan wall-clock time is consumed by LLM inference wait inside the 4-slot batch pool (`SCANNER_ENGINE_POOL_HARD_CAP=4`). In sampled scans, 86/86 decisions exited via `max_turns_exceeded` (40 turns/window across up to 7 reprompt windows = up to 280 turns/worker) because weak proxied models fail the offensive stop-gate `[AGENT osprey-01:REPORT.md; mako-02:WS7-FINAL-REPORT.md]`.
  4. *Real Dominator 2 — Exploit Floor Cell Stranding:* `exploit_floor.py` claims 20 cells per family (`claimed_by="floor-{family}"`) but contains ZERO release calls across 5,285 lines. This strands 1,600 to 7,364 cells per scan under 1,800–6,000 s leases, starving the fleet `[AGENT falcon-01:FINAL_REPORT.md; falcon-02:SYNTHESIS.md; nova-02:FINAL-REPORT.md]`.
  5. *Real Dominator 3 — Provider Failure Rate & Claim-Time Burn:* 53% to 59.5% of `worker_runs` fail on upstream provider errors ("ChatCompletion response has no choices", 429 rate limits). Because `attempts` increments at SQL claim time, 3 consecutive provider dropouts permanently retire a cell as `attempted` without a single probe ever reaching the target `[AGENT orion-01:dossier.md; lynx-03:FINAL_REPORT.md]`.
- **Blast Radius:** Whole-platform scan duration (bloated from 45 min to 15+ hours), concurrency starvation, and false "quiescence" termination.

